From: OpenAI Codex <codex@local>
Subject: econet-eth: include TRGMII resync in delayed MT7530 reapply

Reboot testing on Archer C5v still showed occasional wired Ethernet loss after
the initial TRGMII resync. The delayed work previously only re-applied the
external MT7530 VLAN/port table, which does not recover a dead TRGMII data path
when registers already read back correctly.

Run the TRGMII pad resync before each delayed VLAN split reapply and extend the
retry window to 2s, 10s, 30s, 60s and 120s. Both operations are idempotent for
the C5v VLAN-split path and keep the existing topology unchanged.
---
--- a/econet_eth.c	2026-06-26 09:44:46.860293168 +0300
+++ b/econet_eth.c	2026-06-26 09:45:47.892737025 +0300
@@ -702,7 +702,7 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
-#define EN75_MT7530_REAPPLY_MAX	3
+#define EN75_MT7530_REAPPLY_MAX	5
 
 static unsigned int en75_ext_switch_reapply_delay_ms(unsigned int attempt)
 {
@@ -711,8 +711,12 @@
 		return 2000;
 	case 1:
 		return 10000;
-	default:
+	case 2:
 		return 30000;
+	case 3:
+		return 60000;
+	default:
+		return 120000;
 	}
 }
 
@@ -724,14 +728,20 @@
 	unsigned int attempt = eth->mt7530_reapply_count + 1;
 	int err;
 
+	err = en75_trgmii_resync(eth);
+	if (err)
+		dev_warn(eth->pub.dev,
+			 "failed to re-sync MT7530 TRGMII path attempt %u: %d\n",
+			 attempt, err);
+
 	err = en75_ext_switch_configure_vlan_split(eth);
 	if (err)
 		dev_warn(eth->pub.dev,
-			 "failed to re-apply external MT7530 VLAN split attempt %u: %d\n",
+			 "failed to re-apply external MT7530 TRGMII/VLAN split attempt %u: %d\n",
 			 attempt, err);
 	else
 		dev_info(eth->pub.dev,
-			 "re-applied external MT7530 VLAN split attempt %u/%u\n",
+			 "re-applied external MT7530 TRGMII/VLAN split attempt %u/%u\n",
 			 attempt, EN75_MT7530_REAPPLY_MAX);
 
 	eth->mt7530_reapply_count++;
